:"https://api.github.com/users/bradenmacdonald/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradenmacdonald/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradenmacdonald/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradenmacdonald/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bradenmacdonald","id":945577,"login":"bradenmacdonald","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk0NTU3Nw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradenmacdonald/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradenmacdonald/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradenmacdonald/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradenmacdonald/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradenmacdonald/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradenmacdonald","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/duremaar/chalix-mfe-authoring/commits/bd18e874b572d61a74848dacd71ba4436b0fac2d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-07-17T20:45:22Z","email":"braden@opencraft.com","name":"Braden MacDonald"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-07-17T20:45:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix broken StudioHome tests (#2291)\n\nThere were a ton of problems with these tests, but the main one was the use of `waitFor` without `await`, causing all of the code inside each `waitFor` block to essentially be ignored.\n\nOther problems fixed:\n* Rendering a router inside a router was causing most of the render() calls to fail (our custom `render()` already provides a router so there''s no need to provide one in the test case)\n* Use of `testid` instead of queries based on what users see\n* Tests could match on content in the body when trying to make assertions about the header\n* Mock imported via `index.js` was causing `jest-haste-map` to print warnings about duplicate mock names (this is still happening for other mocks)\n* Passing `courses: null` instead of `courses: []` was causing a broken render on two of the tests.\n\nI also made other cleanups to follow best practices.","tree":{"sha":"0b0e3ff70f61439c743343473b2e203b1d2b6038","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/duremaar/chalix-mfe-authoring/git/trees/0b0e3ff70f61439c743343473b2e203b1d2b6038"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/duremaar/chalix-mfe-authoring/git/commits/bd18e874b572d61a74848dacd71ba4436b0fac2d","verification":{"payload":"tree 0b0e3ff70f61439c743343473b2e203b1d2b6038\nparent 2db6d89fca20cf14c9d2f8cebb0083a7031c074c\nauthor Braden MacDonald <braden@opencraft.com> 1752785122 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1752785122 -0500\n\nFix broken StudioHome tests (#2291)\n\nThere were a ton of problems with these tests, but the main one was the use of `waitFor` without `await`, causing all of the code inside each `waitFor` block to essentially be ignored.\n\nOther problems fixed:\n* Rendering a router inside a router was causing most of the render() calls to fail (our custom `render()` already provides a router so there''s no need to provide one in the test case)\n* Use of `testid` instead of queries based on what users see\n* Tests could match on content in the body when trying to make assertions about the header\n* Mock imported via `index.js` was causing `jest-haste-map` to print warnings about duplicate mock names (this is still happening for other mocks)\n* Passing `courses: null` instead of `courses: []` was causing a broken render on two of the tests.\n\nI also made other cleanups to follow best practices.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJoeWDiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfPkQAGiwg3rpL2gNlmWFujsZmMrJ\n4sj+Wha2X9IPKYrYtb1VWzEyzKpJBAfC2jfn8U0P+6qLefgjya7/XFXvb1RM0S8x\nn0nS+VJIHFFsAd3lt1dJsa3No6rlMerWqq6CiNLTh+wRcTU4oihP8eMREWCoKrR9\nTzWuHjcg0fkJtSPLWoNMMmwCmW4XmfJnmVA7uKLALv8f5qisFBDHwx+LOEAvKo+w\no/AYVAf7fJ2rexHvQ/p3FIpSb57bz5Jmbcrg93giGRR2